  "notes": "A compound of {潜|せん} (to dive, to lurk) and {水|すい} (water).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {潜水艦|せんすいかん} (submarine)\n- {潜水|せんすい}{士|し} (professional diver)\n- {潜水|せんすい}{服|ふく} (diving suit)\n- スキューバ{潜水|せんすい} (scuba diving)\n- {潜水|せんすい}{時間|じかん} (dive time / submersion time)\n\nFor recreational scuba diving, ダイビング is more commonly used in casual speech. {潜水|せんすい} has a more formal or technical tone and is standard in military and professional contexts.",
